      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Taking 600mg of Advil with a large meal is a common dose, but since you have a history of stomach sensitivity, I strongly advise against self-medicating this way. Because your pain is severe, consider alternating doses of acetaminophen (Tylenol) with Advil, as they work differently in the body. For immediate relief tonight, try a cool compress on the outside of your cheek to help reduce inflammation while you wait for your appointment.",
